## What the legacy shell asserted and where it lives now

- **The shell itself** (C01 rail, topbar, palette, Settings tabs): C35 (`acceptance_c35.py`, C35-N01..N03) and C44-N01.
- **Settings' "Use the new interface" switch** (C28, C35): removed; C44-N01 asserts its absence. The core accepts `setUiVariant` and ignores it (`ui_v2_closure`).
- **Runtime Security, AI Gateway, Red Team & Models as pages** (C03, C09, C10, C13, C16–C18): Administration's product cards (C39); the Go/palette entries open the product in Administration (`ui_v2_closure`, C44-N01).
- **Sessions & Reports** (C11) and **Import from v1** (C23): framed by the v2 shell as before; no board of their own in P09. C44-N01 opens each.
- **The Academy destination** (C04–C07): the v2 Academy chrome around the same learner pages (C42); the learner suites under `features/academy/*.test.tsx` now exercise the v2 component.
- **The API Client** (C14, C15) and **the Library** (C12): C41 and C40.
- **The Harness** (C19–C22): C38.
- **Privacy, diagnostics and network** (C24): C44-N01 repeats the no-plaintext-secret sweep over the whole-app capture set.

## Files removed in C44

`apps/desktop/src/shell/desktop-shell.tsx` (+test), `command-palette.tsx`, `icons.ts`; `features/academy/academy-view.tsx` (+test), `features/administration/administration-view.tsx`, `features/red-team/red-team-view.tsx` (+test), `features/runtime/runtime-view.tsx`, `features/runtime/overview-inbox.tsx` (+test); the `Interface` fieldset of Settings; the legacy branch of `app.tsx` and `feature-body.tsx`.

## Legacy suites retired with the shell, and the two that run again on the one presentation

`features/administration/administration-view.test.tsx` (the legacy Administration view's inventories: the v2 Administration suite covers paging, denied refresh, context replacement, the review sheet and the inventories through the v2 imports). The DLP authoring suite is ported, assertion for assertion, to `v2/admin/dlp-authoring.test.tsx` (the Runtime card's DLP tab and its inventory radios; the review sheet hosts the change workbench): v1's actions per inventory, the dictionary draft from typed keywords, a chosen file by its token only, the whole-list replace on edit, typed keywords kept when a choice is cancelled or fails, and metadata that must be one JSON object. The management-client onboarding suite (the owner's uncommitted `features/tenants/management-credential.test.tsx`, excluded) is ported to `v2/settings/management-credential.test.tsx`: the secret cleared before awaiting and kept out of storage, the required fields, the TSG requirement, the SSO pointer, verification as one management read with faithful failures, and removal of the management client only.

## Files kept although no v2 screen imports them

The owner's uncommitted work (docs/planning/evidence/C28/owner-work.json) touches `features/gateway/gateway-view.tsx`, `playground.tsx`, `features/harness/harness-view.tsx`, `sign-in-panel.tsx`, `prerequisites.tsx`, `features/library/library-view.tsx`, `features/workbench/workbench-view.tsx` and their tests; deleting them on this branch would collide with that work, so they and the components only they import (`gateway-files.tsx`, `gateway-observe.tsx`, the Harness panels, `document-editor.tsx`, `request-send.tsx`) stay as unreferenced code until the owner's work lands. Their tests still run.

## C39a attempt-01 remediation carried in C44

- R1: below 760 CSS px the inventory rows stack their cells (`tokens.css`), and `acceptance_c39.py`'s layout predicate fails on any two texts of the table drawn over each other, beyond containment.
- R2: Close details retires the read in flight and the opened item (`inventory-table.tsx`); a regression test keeps the panel closed and focus stable after a late reply and a later refresh.
- R3: the empty search says it searched the page that was read and points at First page / Next page (`copy.ts`); a two-page regression test with the match on the other page.
- E2: `administration.test.tsx` adds the v2 Playground's submit (refused, unconfirmed, admitted), cancel and save-case handlers and the table's paging, denied refresh and context replacement through the v2 imports.
# C44 parity notes — closure (no board)

C44 has no prototype board of its own: it removes the legacy shell and closes the phase. `parity/app/<destination>-{light,dark}.png` is the whole-app screenshot set `tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c44.py` captures from every destination the catalogue lists, against the bundle in `native-prepare.json`; each screen's own board composite is under its chunk (C35–C43). The destinations without a board (Sessions & Reports, Import from v1, Settings) are the C11/C23/C02 views framed by the v2 shell, unchanged.

## What changed, and why

- **One presentation.** The core's snapshot always says `v2` with the v2 catalogue; an older store's persisted `legacy` is ignored; `setUiVariant` is accepted and ignored so older presentations and drivers are not refused. The Settings "Interface" switch, the legacy shell (`desktop-shell.tsx`, its palette and icons) and the legacy feature views no v2 screen imports are removed; the owner's uncommitted legacy files stay (legacy-script-map.md lists them).
- **The product destinations** (Runtime Security, AI Gateway, Red Team & Models in Go and the palette) open Administration on their product rather than the legacy pages.
- **The first run is the wizard**, so the native drivers' tenant setup walks it once (`v2_setup.py`) and adds the synthetic-endpoint tenant through Settings' tenant form.

## Owner's judgement

Recorded 2026-10-30: the owner directed the gates to proceed without a per-screen pause ("go go gog og o go gog o. stop stopping. go go go go go until we are 100% complete. stop stopping. go go go go go", "please continue my guy", "done. do it", "no matter what autonomy I give you, you keep stopping"). The screenshot set is posted for the record; that direction is the judgement this gate runs on; an objection reopens the chunk.

